# Title: Regsvr32 Execution From Potential Suspicious Location
# ID: 9525dc73-0327-438c-8c04-13c0e037e9da
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2023-05-26
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1218.010
# Description: Detects execution of regsvr32 where the DLL is located in a potentially suspicious location.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_exec="*:\\ProgramData\\*" OR process_exec="*:\\Temp\\*" OR process_exec="*:\\Users\\Public\\*" OR process_exec="*:\\Windows\\Temp\\*" OR process_exec="*\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\*" OR process_exec="*\\AppData\\Roaming\\*")) AND ((process_path="*\\regsvr32.exe") OR (process_name="REGSVR32.EXE")))
